WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:09.101
This is chalkcast. You will teach a problem on a whiteboard, while your camera and your voice are recorded. Here is how it works.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:17.757
Before you start, use a computer with Chrome, Edge, or Safari. You will need a camera and a microphone.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:25.869
If you have an accommodation or a privacy concern, contact your instructor before you record.

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:30.876
Open the link in your assignment, and press Start.

00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:37.561
Your instructor's problem is already filled in. Read it, then press Next.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:43.877
Press Turn on camera and mic. When your browser asks, choose Allow.

00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:51.991
Check that you can see yourself, and that the gold bar moves when you talk. Then go to the whiteboard.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.079
The whiteboard opens, but you are not recording yet. You can try the tools first.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.308
When you are ready, press Record.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.480
A short countdown gives you a moment to get ready.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.433
Then draw, and explain your thinking out loud.

00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:21.339
Talk through each step, the way you would teach a classmate.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:28.049
Pick a tool on the left. The colors and the size are just below the tools.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:36.605
To add typed text, choose Text, and click the board. Type your words, then press Return to place them.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:44.020
Use Move to drag an item to a new spot. To resize it, drag its gold dot.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:50.664
Above the board, you can add a page, zoom in, undo, or add a picture.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.441
Check off each rubric item as you cover it.

00:01:57.433 --> 00:02:01.381
If you need a moment, press Pause. When you are done, press Finish.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:08.787
Watch your video once to check the sound. Then name it with the topic and your initials.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.849
Next, download your video.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.625
Then download your whiteboard PDF.

00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:24.328
Last, upload both files to your assignment, the way your instructions say.

00:02:26.333 --> 00:02:35.188
Sometimes your instructor will send a link for an assignment defense. That is a short follow-up question about work you already turned in.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.361
The first screen explains how it works. Read it before you begin.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:49.000
After the camera check, you can practice on the whiteboard. Your question is not showing yet.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:03:03.609
When you press Begin Defense, your question appears, and recording starts at the same moment. You get one attempt, and you cannot pause or restart. Then download and upload your files as usual.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:16.823
Two things that are good to know. Your video stays on your own device until you upload it. And if you close the tab by accident, open the link again, and your work will be waiting.

00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:21.651
That is everything. You are ready to record.
